
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
DA = DB [00]
DB = DC [01]
DE = DA [02]
BE ⟂ AC [03]
A,F,B are collinear [04]
FB = FA [05]
A,G,C are collinear [06]
E,B,G are collinear [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. DA = DB [00] & DE = DA [02] & DB = DC [01] ⇒  E,A,B,C are concyclic [08]
002. E,A,B,C are concyclic [08] ⇒  ∠ABE = ∠ACE [09]
003. A,G,C are collinear [06] & E,B,G are collinear [07] & AC ⟂ BE [03] ⇒  AG ⟂ GB [10]
004. A,F,B are collinear [04] & FB = FA [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of BA [11]
005. AG ⟂ GB [10] & F is midpoint of BA [11] ⇒  BF = GF [12]
006. BF = GF [12] ⇒  ∠FBG = ∠BGF [13]
007. A,G,C are collinear [06] & ∠ABE = ∠ACE [09] & ∠FBG = ∠BGF [13] & A,F,B are collinear [04] & E,B,G are collinear [07] ⇒  ∠(EB-FG) = ∠(AG-EC) [14]
008. A,G,C are collinear [06] & AC ⟂ BE [03] ⇒  AG ⟂ EB [15]
009. ∠(EB-FG) = ∠(AG-EC) [14] & AG ⟂ EB [15] ⇒  CE ⟂ FG
